Question 03 (b) – Class Identification Using Five Rules

## Five Rules Used:

1. Redundant Classes – Remove nouns that represent the same concept.
2. Attribute Classes – Remove nouns that represent properties of other classes.
3. Irrelevant Classes – Remove nouns outside the system scope or unnecessary implementation details.
4. Vague Classes – Remove nouns that do not represent clearly defined objects.
5. Operation Classes – Remove nouns that represent actions rather than independent entities.

